exports[`G-PROMPT-E02 — Pass 2 built prompts (indoor) > pass2: mid-century × kitchen 1`] = `"Edit this photo of a finished room. Walls, floor, ceiling are final — keep them unchanged. Same camera angle. Room dimensions FIXED — do not stretch or compress. Columns visible — do not hide with furniture. Keep the input's color temperature. No curtains, no drapes. If the room is narrow or compact, preserve that — reduce furniture count rather than widening walls.  Keep all fixed equipment (radiators, convectors, heaters, vents, panels, towel dryers) — same count, same positions. No furniture blocking them. No new architectural elements (arches, niches, columns, coffers, windows, doors) unless already in the input. ADD kitchen elements: Kitchen accessories and freestanding elements ONLY — preserve all existing kitchen built-in cabinetry (upper and lower cabinets), appliances (oven, cooktop, hob, range, fridge, dishwasher, microwave, hood, extractor fan), countertops, sink, faucet, and backsplash exactly as they appear in the input photo: same position, same size, same finish, same layout. Do NOT replace them, do NOT relocate them, do NOT add a second oven, a second cooktop, a second sink, or new cabinetry. ADD only freestanding and decorative accessories: a small cutting board 30cm on the countertop, a ceramic utensil jar 15cm with wooden spoons, a fruit bowl 25cm with seasonal fruit, a folded tea towel in a neutral tone, a small potted herb 12cm in a terracotta pot ONLY if a windowsill or free shelf is visible, a cookbook stand 20cm with an open cookbook ONLY if counter space allows. If — and only if — the input clearly shows a visible island or peninsula with no stools in front of it, add two or three bar stools 75cm seat height matching the style materials. If — and only if — the input clearly shows a dedicated dining zone within the kitchen (open floor area away from work zones) with no table visible, add a small dining table 100cm wide with 4 chairs matching the style. If — and only if — the input shows a visible island or peninsula with no pendant light above it, add one or two pendant lights 30-40cm matching the style — otherwise the ceiling light from pass 1 stays as the only overhead fixture. Functional and organized atmosphere — counters kept mostly clear, no clutter, no armchairs, no lounge chairs, no floor lamps, no area rug on the work zone. Design style: mid century. Materials and palette: Warm walnut wood, mustard and teal woven fabrics, brass and black metal, natural linen, tapered legs, organic curves, terracotta planters.. Cabinetry against walls. Island only if >10m2. Ceiling light from pass 1 — keep as-is. Scale to apparent width. Distribute kitchen elements across the full depth. Work zones along walls, island in middle if >10m2. Counter accessories spread across full counter length. Include 2-3 lived-in details: cutting board, fruit bowl, folded tea towel. Luxury listing photo. Contact shadows on every piece. DSLR wide-angle, sharp focus, deep DOF. Same focal length as input. No text. Freestanding objects only — place furniture INSIDE the room only, not on terraces or balconies visible through windows."`;

